Why a language model gives the answer it gives can usually only be estimated. Explanations of neural networks are mostly computed after training and approximate what the model did, and
for language models the most visible quantity, the attention weights, need not explain the output [ 1 , 2 ] . A model that is right for the wrong reasons looks, from its accuracy,
the same as one that is right for the right ones.

